#set($h2 = '##')
# ${SERVER_NAME}

A standalone MCP server that connects to an Oracle database and exposes SQL queries as tools
over STDIO transport. Designed to work with MCP clients such as Claude Desktop.

$h2 Tools

#foreach($tool in $TOOLS)
- **${tool.name}** — ${tool.description}
#end

$h2 Running

```
java -jar ${JAR_NAME}
```

The `${ENV_NAME}` file must be in the same directory as the JAR.

$h2 Security

The `${ENV_NAME}` file contains your database credentials:

```
${ENV_PREFIX}_DB_USER=...
${ENV_PREFIX}_DB_PASSWORD=...
```

- Do **not** commit this file to version control — add it to `.gitignore`
- Restrict file permissions: `chmod 600 ${ENV_NAME}`
- The password is Base64-encoded (prefixed with `base64:`) — it is **not** encrypted

$h2 Claude Desktop

Add the following to your `claude_desktop_config.json`:

```json
{
  "mcpServers": {
    "${SERVER_NAME}": {
      "command": "java",
      "args": ["-jar", "/absolute/path/to/${JAR_NAME}"]
    }
  }
}
```
